{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"gpu","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":143716}],"dockerImageVersionId":31400,"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":true}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"18fe7bc2","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n# Smart MCQ Solver — Main Notebook (v2: targeting higher MAP@3)\n### DL & GenAI Project — 3-Model Pipeline (Scratch + Pretrained + Fine-tuned) + Retrieval + Ensemble\n\nChanges from v1, all legitimate (no test-label leakage):\n1. **Model 3 upgraded** `deberta-v3-small` → **`deberta-v3-large`**.\n2. **Retrieval-augmented context** added to Model 3's input (Milestone 3's RAG requirement, and\n   the single biggest lever for knowledge-style MCQs).\n3. **5-fold GroupKFold cross-validation** for Models 1 and 3, so ensemble weights are fit on\n   out-of-fold predictions covering the *entire* training set instead of one 15% holdout —\n   more reliable weights, and a small honest MAP@3 gain from better calibration.\n4. **Finer ensemble weight search** (0.05 step via `scipy.optimize`) at the end.\n\nModel 2 stays zero-shot (no training → no fold-leakage risk, scored once on the full train set).\n\n**You will need a text corpus for retrieval.** Point `CORPUS_PATH` at a passages file\n(e.g. a Wikipedia-passages Kaggle dataset — search Kaggle Datasets for one matching your\nquestion domain, or your instructor may provide one). If none is available, set\n`USE_RETRIEVAL = False` and Model 3 will just use prompt+options like v1 — you'll get the\nmodel-size/CV gains but not the retrieval gain.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"9c35f730","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 0. Setup","metadata":{}},{"id":"d7fc9eae","cell_type":"code","source":"!pip install -q -U wandb sentence-transformers peft accelerate transformers evaluate scikit-learn scipy\n!pip uninstall -y -q torchao\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"5f314a3a","cell_type":"code","source":"\nimport os, re, json, math, gc\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import GroupKFold\nfrom sklearn.metrics import f1_score\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\nSEED = 42\nnp.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED)\nDEVICE = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\nprint('Device:', DEVICE)\n\nOPTS = ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E']\nOPT2IDX = {o: i for i, o in enumerate(OPTS)}\nN_FOLDS = 5\n\nTRAIN_PATH  = '/kaggle/input/competitions/smart-mcq-solver-challenge/train.csv'   # <-- update path\nTEST_PATH   = '/kaggle/input/competitions/smart-mcq-solver-challenge/test.csv'    # <-- update path\nUSE_RETRIEVAL = True\nCORPUS_PATH = '/kaggle/input/your-wikipedia-passages-dataset/passages.parquet'    # <-- update path\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"7161aa62","cell_type":"code","source":"\nimport wandb\nfrom kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n\nWANDB_PROJECT = \"23f2003210-t22026\"\nWANDB_ENTITY  = \"23f2003210-indian-institute-of-technology-madras\"\n\nuser_secrets = UserSecretsClient()\nwandb_key = user_secrets.get_secret(\"WANDB_API_KEY\")\nwandb.login(key=wandb_key)\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"b1b5c6a4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Load & Clean Data","metadata":{}},{"id":"e6276c91","cell_type":"code","source":"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(TRAIN_PATH)\ntest  = pd.read_csv(TEST_PATH)\n\ndef clean(t):\n    t = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', str(t)).strip()\n    return t\n\nfor c in ['prompt'] + OPTS:\n    train[c] = train[c].astype(str).map(clean)\n    test[c]  = test[c].astype(str).map(clean)\n\nopt_cols = ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E']\ntrain['opt_key'] = train[opt_cols].astype(str).agg('|'.join, axis=1)  # group key, prevents fold leakage\nytr_full = train['answer'].map(OPT2IDX).values\n\nprint(train.shape, test.shape)\ntrain.head(2)\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"8ac7c52b","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. MAP@3 Metric & Shared Helpers","metadata":{}},{"id":"f7f197c0","cell_type":"code","source":"\ndef map_at_3(scores, y_true):\n    order = np.argsort(-scores, axis=1)[:, :3]\n    ap = 0.0\n    for i in range(len(y_true)):\n        hits = np.where(order[i] == y_true[i])[0]\n        if len(hits):\n            ap += 1.0 / (hits[0] + 1)\n    return ap / len(y_true)\n\ndef top3_labels(scores):\n    order = np.argsort(-scores, axis=1)[:, :3]\n    return [' '.join(OPTS[j] for j in row) for row in order]\n\ndef top1_metrics(scores, y_true):\n    preds = scores.argmax(axis=1)\n    acc = (preds == y_true).mean()\n    f1 = f1_score(y_true, preds, average='macro')\n    return acc, f1\n\ngkf = GroupKFold(n_splits=N_FOLDS)\nfold_indices = list(gkf.split(train, groups=train['opt_key']))\nprint(f\"{N_FOLDS}-fold GroupKFold ready, fold sizes:\", [len(v) for _, v in fold_indices])\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"b339537b","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 3. MODEL 1 — From Scratch: TF-IDF/SVD + MLP, trained with 5-fold CV\n\nSame architecture as v1. Now trained once per fold; out-of-fold (OOF) predictions cover\n100% of the training set (vs. 15% before), and test predictions are averaged across folds\n(a free ensembling effect on its own).\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"bdfb66c4","cell_type":"code","source":"\ntfidf = TfidfVectorizer(max_features=20000, ngram_range=(1, 2), sublinear_tf=True)\nall_texts = list(train['prompt']) + [t for c in OPTS for t in train[c]]\ntfidf.fit(all_texts)\n\nsvd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=128, random_state=SEED)\nsvd.fit(tfidf.transform(all_texts))\n\ndef embed(texts):\n    return svd.transform(tfidf.transform(texts))\n\ndef build_features(df):\n    p_emb = embed(df['prompt'].tolist())\n    feats = []\n    for opt in OPTS:\n        o_emb = embed(df[opt].tolist())\n        prod = p_emb * o_emb\n        diff = np.abs(p_emb - o_emb)\n        cos = (p_emb * o_emb).sum(1) / (np.linalg.norm(p_emb, axis=1) * np.linalg.norm(o_emb, axis=1) + 1e-8)\n        feats.append(np.concatenate([p_emb, o_emb, prod, diff, cos[:, None]], axis=1))\n    return np.stack(feats, axis=1)\n\nX_full = build_features(train)\nX_test_m1 = build_features(test)\nprint(\"feature shape:\", X_full.shape)\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"5e812e46","cell_type":"code","source":"\nclass ScratchScorer(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, in_dim, hidden=128):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(in_dim, hidden), nn.ReLU(), nn.Dropout(0.3),\n            nn.Linear(hidden, hidden // 2), nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Linear(hidden // 2, 1),\n        )\n    def forward(self, x):\n        B, K, Fd = x.shape\n        return self.net(x.reshape(B * K, Fd)).reshape(B, K)\n\nrun1 = wandb.init(project=WANDB_PROJECT, entity=WANDB_ENTITY, name=\"model1_scratch_tfidf_mlp_cv\",\n                   job_type=\"train\", config={\"hidden\": 128, \"epochs\": 30, \"lr\": 1e-3, \"batch_size\": 64, \"n_folds\": N_FOLDS})\ncfg1 = run1.config\n\noof_probs_m1 = np.zeros((len(train), 5))\ntest_probs_m1_folds = []\n\nfor fold, (tr_idx, va_idx) in enumerate(fold_indices):\n    model1 = ScratchScorer(X_full.shape[-1], cfg1.hidden).to(DEVICE)\n    opt1 = torch.optim.Adam(model1.parameters(), lr=cfg1.lr, weight_decay=1e-5)\n    Xtr_t = torch.tensor(X_full[tr_idx], dtype=torch.float32)\n    ytr_t = torch.tensor(ytr_full[tr_idx], dtype=torch.long)\n    Xva_t = torch.tensor(X_full[va_idx], dtype=torch.float32)\n\n    for epoch in range(cfg1.epochs):\n        model1.train()\n        perm = torch.randperm(len(Xtr_t))\n        for i in range(0, len(perm), cfg1.batch_size):\n            idx = perm[i:i + cfg1.batch_size]\n            xb, yb = Xtr_t[idx].to(DEVICE), ytr_t[idx].to(DEVICE)\n            loss = F.cross_entropy(model1(xb), yb)\n            opt1.zero_grad(); loss.backward(); opt1.step()\n\n    model1.eval()\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        va_scores = model1(Xva_t.to(DEVICE)).cpu().numpy()\n        test_scores = model1(torch.tensor(X_test_m1, dtype=torch.float32).to(DEVICE)).cpu().numpy()\n    oof_probs_m1[va_idx] = F.softmax(torch.tensor(va_scores), dim=1).numpy()\n    test_probs_m1_folds.append(F.softmax(torch.tensor(test_scores), dim=1).numpy())\n\n    fold_m3 = map_at_3(va_scores, ytr_full[va_idx])\n    wandb.log({\"fold\": fold, \"fold_val_map3\": fold_m3})\n    print(f\"Fold {fold}: val MAP@3 = {fold_m3:.4f}\")\n\ntest_probs_m1 = np.mean(test_probs_m1_folds, axis=0)\noof_m3_m1 = map_at_3(oof_probs_m1, ytr_full)\noof_acc_m1, oof_f1_m1 = top1_metrics(oof_probs_m1, ytr_full)\nprint(\"Model 1 OOF MAP@3:\", oof_m3_m1, \"| acc:\", oof_acc_m1, \"| F1:\", oof_f1_m1)\nrun1.summary[\"oof_map3\"] = oof_m3_m1\nrun1.summary[\"oof_acc\"] = oof_acc_m1\nrun1.summary[\"oof_f1\"] = oof_f1_m1\nrun1.finish()\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"89ba23bc","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 4. MODEL 2 — Pretrained (Zero-shot): Sentence-Transformer Embeddings\n\nZero-shot, no training → no leakage risk from scoring the full train set directly.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"bfcdd55a","cell_type":"code","source":"\nrun2 = wandb.init(project=WANDB_PROJECT, entity=WANDB_ENTITY, name=\"model2_pretrained_minilm\",\n                   job_type=\"eval\", config={\"model\": \"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"})\n\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nst_model = SentenceTransformer(run2.config.model, device=DEVICE)\n\ndef st_scores(df):\n    prompts = df['prompt'].tolist()\n    p_emb = st_model.encode(prompts, batch_size=64, show_progress_bar=True, normalize_embeddings=True)\n    scores = np.zeros((len(df), 5))\n    for j, opt in enumerate(OPTS):\n        o_emb = st_model.encode(df[opt].tolist(), batch_size=64, show_progress_bar=True, normalize_embeddings=True)\n        scores[:, j] = (p_emb * o_emb).sum(1)\n    return scores\n\ntrain_scores_m2 = st_scores(train)\ntest_scores_m2 = st_scores(test)\noof_probs_m2 = F.softmax(torch.tensor(train_scores_m2) * 10, dim=1).numpy()\ntest_probs_m2 = F.softmax(torch.tensor(test_scores_m2) * 10, dim=1).numpy()\n\noof_m3_m2 = map_at_3(oof_probs_m2, ytr_full)\noof_acc_m2, oof_f1_m2 = top1_metrics(oof_probs_m2, ytr_full)\nprint(\"Model 2 MAP@3:\", oof_m3_m2, \"| acc:\", oof_acc_m2, \"| F1:\", oof_f1_m2)\nrun2.summary[\"oof_map3\"] = oof_m3_m2\nrun2.summary[\"oof_acc\"] = oof_acc_m2\nrun2.summary[\"oof_f1\"] = oof_f1_m2\nrun2.finish()\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"65663e8c","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 5. Retrieval-Augmented Context (for Model 3)\n\nRetrieves the top-k most relevant passages for each question from a text corpus using\nMiniLM embeddings (reusing the model above), and concatenates them into Model 3's input.\nThis targets Milestone 3 (RAG) directly and is usually worth more MAP@3 than any single\narchitecture change for knowledge-heavy MCQs.\n\nSkip this section (`USE_RETRIEVAL = False`) if you don't have a suitable corpus — Model 3\nwill still work, just without the extra context.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"af072e45","cell_type":"code","source":"\ndef build_retriever(corpus_path):\n    corpus_df = pd.read_parquet(corpus_path) if corpus_path.endswith('.parquet') else pd.read_csv(corpus_path)\n    passages = corpus_df['text'].astype(str).tolist()   # <-- adjust column name to your corpus\n    passage_emb = st_model.encode(passages, batch_size=128, show_progress_bar=True,\n                                   normalize_embeddings=True, convert_to_numpy=True)\n    return passages, passage_emb\n\ndef retrieve_context(df, passages, passage_emb, top_k=2):\n    q_emb = st_model.encode(df['prompt'].tolist(), batch_size=64, show_progress_bar=True,\n                             normalize_embeddings=True, convert_to_numpy=True)\n    sims = q_emb @ passage_emb.T\n    top_idx = np.argsort(-sims, axis=1)[:, :top_k]\n    contexts = [' '.join(passages[j] for j in row) for row in top_idx]\n    return contexts\n\nif USE_RETRIEVAL:\n    passages, passage_emb = build_retriever(CORPUS_PATH)\n    train['context'] = retrieve_context(train, passages, passage_emb, top_k=2)\n    test['context']  = retrieve_context(test, passages, passage_emb, top_k=2)\nelse:\n    train['context'] = ''\n    test['context']  = ''\n\ntrain['prompt_ctx'] = (train['context'] + ' ' + train['prompt']).str.strip()\ntest['prompt_ctx']  = (test['context'] + ' ' + test['prompt']).str.strip()\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"e3008d72","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 6. MODEL 3 — Additional Model: LoRA Fine-tuned `deberta-v3-large`, with retrieved context, 5-fold CV\n\nUpgraded from `deberta-v3-small`. Larger model + longer context needs a smaller per-device\nbatch size — gradient accumulation keeps the effective batch size the same as v1.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"fe279d0a","cell_type":"code","source":"\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForMultipleChoice, TrainingArguments, Trainer\nfrom peft import LoraConfig, get_peft_model, TaskType\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom transformers.tokenization_utils_base import PreTrainedTokenizerBase\nfrom typing import Union\nfrom datasets import Dataset\n\nBASE_MODEL = \"microsoft/deberta-v3-large\"\nMAX_LEN = 384          # bigger, to fit retrieved context + prompt + option\nLORA_R, LORA_ALPHA, LORA_DROPOUT = 8, 16, 0.05\nEPOCHS = 3\nLR = 1e-4\nPER_DEVICE_BS = 2      # smaller: deberta-v3-large is much bigger than v1's -small\nGRAD_ACCUM = 4         # effective batch size = 2 * 4 = 8, matching v1\n\ntok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(BASE_MODEL)\n\ndef to_mc_features(df, has_label=True):\n    first_sentences = sum([[p] * 5 for p in df['prompt_ctx']], [])\n    second_sentences = sum([[df.iloc[i][opt] for opt in OPTS] for i in range(len(df))], [])\n    tokenized = tok(first_sentences, second_sentences, truncation=True, max_length=MAX_LEN, padding='max_length')\n    features = {k: [v[i:i + 5] for i in range(0, len(v), 5)] for k, v in tokenized.items()}\n    if has_label:\n        features['labels'] = df['answer'].map(OPT2IDX).tolist()\n    return features\n\n@dataclass\nclass DataCollatorForMultipleChoice:\n    tokenizer: PreTrainedTokenizerBase\n    padding: Union[bool, str] = True\n    def __call__(self, features):\n        labels = [f.pop(\"labels\") for f in features] if \"labels\" in features[0] else None\n        batch_size, num_choices = len(features), len(features[0][\"input_ids\"])\n        flattened = [{k: v[i] for k, v in f.items()} for f in features for i in range(num_choices)]\n        batch = self.tokenizer.pad(flattened, padding=self.padding, return_tensors=\"pt\")\n        batch = {k: v.view(batch_size, num_choices, -1) for k, v in batch.items()}\n        if labels is not None:\n            batch[\"labels\"] = torch.tensor(labels, dtype=torch.int64)\n        return batch\n\ncollator = DataCollatorForMultipleChoice(tokenizer=tok)\n\ndef compute_metrics(eval_pred):\n    logits, labels = eval_pred\n    scores = torch.softmax(torch.tensor(logits), dim=1).numpy()\n    preds = scores.argmax(1)\n    return {\"map3\": map_at_3(scores, labels), \"accuracy\": (preds == labels).mean(),\n            \"f1\": f1_score(labels, preds, average='macro')}\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"c89d5fd4","cell_type":"code","source":"\nrun3 = wandb.init(project=WANDB_PROJECT, entity=WANDB_ENTITY, name=\"model3_lora_deberta_large_cv\",\n                   job_type=\"train\", config={\"base_model\": BASE_MODEL, \"max_len\": MAX_LEN,\n                                              \"lora_r\": LORA_R, \"epochs\": EPOCHS, \"lr\": LR, \"n_folds\": N_FOLDS})\n\ntest_ds = Dataset.from_dict(to_mc_features(test, has_label=False))\noof_probs_m3 = np.zeros((len(train), 5))\ntest_probs_m3_folds = []\n\nfor fold, (tr_idx, va_idx) in enumerate(fold_indices):\n    tr_fold_df = train.iloc[tr_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n    va_fold_df = train.iloc[va_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n    train_ds = Dataset.from_dict(to_mc_features(tr_fold_df))\n    val_ds   = Dataset.from_dict(to_mc_features(va_fold_df))\n\n    base_model = AutoModelForMultipleChoice.from_pretrained(BASE_MODEL)\n    lora_config = LoraConfig(task_type=TaskType.SEQ_CLS, r=LORA_R, lora_alpha=LORA_ALPHA,\n                              lora_dropout=LORA_DROPOUT, target_modules=[\"query_proj\", \"key_proj\", \"value_proj\"],\n                              modules_to_save=[\"pooler\", \"classifier\"])\n    fold_model = get_peft_model(base_model, lora_config)\n\n    args = TrainingArguments(\n        output_dir=f\"./m3_fold{fold}\", per_device_train_batch_size=PER_DEVICE_BS,\n        per_device_eval_batch_size=PER_DEVICE_BS * 2, gradient_accumulation_steps=GRAD_ACCUM,\n        learning_rate=LR, num_train_epochs=EPOCHS, eval_strategy=\"epoch\", save_strategy=\"no\",\n        report_to=\"none\", run_name=f\"model3_fold{fold}\",\n        bf16=torch.cuda.is_available() and torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n    )\n    trainer = Trainer(model=fold_model, args=args, train_dataset=train_ds, eval_dataset=val_ds,\n                       data_collator=collator, processing_class=tok, compute_metrics=compute_metrics)\n    trainer.train()\n\n    val_logits = trainer.predict(val_ds).predictions\n    val_probs = torch.softmax(torch.tensor(val_logits), dim=1).numpy()\n    oof_probs_m3[va_idx] = val_probs\n\n    test_logits = trainer.predict(test_ds).predictions\n    test_probs_m3_folds.append(torch.softmax(torch.tensor(test_logits), dim=1).numpy())\n\n    fold_m3_score = map_at_3(val_probs, ytr_full[va_idx])\n    wandb.log({\"fold\": fold, \"fold_val_map3\": fold_m3_score})\n    print(f\"Fold {fold}: val MAP@3 = {fold_m3_score:.4f}\")\n\n    del base_model, fold_model, trainer\n    gc.collect(); torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n\ntest_probs_m3 = np.mean(test_probs_m3_folds, axis=0)\noof_m3_m3 = map_at_3(oof_probs_m3, ytr_full)\noof_acc_m3, oof_f1_m3 = top1_metrics(oof_probs_m3, ytr_full)\nprint(\"Model 3 OOF MAP@3:\", oof_m3_m3, \"| acc:\", oof_acc_m3, \"| F1:\", oof_f1_m3)\nrun3.summary[\"oof_map3\"] = oof_m3_m3\nrun3.summary[\"oof_acc\"] = oof_acc_m3\nrun3.summary[\"oof_f1\"] = oof_f1_m3\nrun3.finish()\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"4dff5523","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Compare All 3 Models in W&B (OOF metrics — covers 100% of training data)","metadata":{}},{"id":"ebcdc8f7","cell_type":"code","source":"\ncompare_run = wandb.init(project=WANDB_PROJECT, entity=WANDB_ENTITY, name=\"model_comparison_cv\", job_type=\"eval\")\ntable = wandb.Table(columns=[\"model\", \"type\", \"oof_map3\", \"oof_accuracy\", \"oof_f1\"], data=[\n    [\"Model 1 - TF-IDF/SVD + MLP\", \"From scratch\", oof_m3_m1, oof_acc_m1, oof_f1_m1],\n    [\"Model 2 - MiniLM (SentenceTransformers)\", \"Pretrained (zero-shot)\", oof_m3_m2, oof_acc_m2, oof_f1_m2],\n    [\"Model 3 - DeBERTa-v3-large + LoRA + RAG\", \"Additional (fine-tuned)\", oof_m3_m3, oof_acc_m3, oof_f1_m3],\n])\ncompare_run.log({\"model_comparison\": table})\ncompare_run.finish()\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"40f815cd","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 8. Ensemble (fit on OOF predictions, fine-grained weight search) & Final Submission\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"9980f810","cell_type":"code","source":"\ndef ensemble_probs(w, p1, p2, p3):\n    w1, w2, w3 = w\n    return w1 * p1 + w2 * p2 + w3 * p3\n\ndef neg_map3(w):\n    w = np.clip(w, 0, None)\n    w = w / (w.sum() + 1e-9)\n    probs = ensemble_probs(w, oof_probs_m1, oof_probs_m2, oof_probs_m3)\n    return -map_at_3(probs, ytr_full)\n\nres = minimize(neg_map3, x0=[1/3, 1/3, 1/3], method='Nelder-Mead',\n                options={'xatol': 1e-3, 'fatol': 1e-4, 'maxiter': 500})\nw = np.clip(res.x, 0, None); w = w / w.sum()\nw1, w2, w3 = w\nprint(\"Best ensemble weights (m1, m2, m3):\", w, \"| OOF MAP@3:\", -res.fun)\n\noof_probs_ens = ensemble_probs(w, oof_probs_m1, oof_probs_m2, oof_probs_m3)\nens_acc, ens_f1 = top1_metrics(oof_probs_ens, ytr_full)\nprint(\"Ensemble OOF acc:\", ens_acc, \"| OOF F1:\", ens_f1)\n\nens_run = wandb.init(project=WANDB_PROJECT, entity=WANDB_ENTITY, name=\"ensemble_final_cv\", job_type=\"eval\",\n                      config={\"w1\": float(w1), \"w2\": float(w2), \"w3\": float(w3)})\nens_run.summary[\"oof_map3\"] = -res.fun\nens_run.summary[\"oof_acc\"] = ens_acc\nens_run.summary[\"oof_f1\"] = ens_f1\nens_run.finish()\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"4b00c87d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 9. Validation Error Analysis (on OOF predictions — covers every training row)\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"374ef321","cell_type":"code","source":"\noof_order = np.argsort(-oof_probs_ens, axis=1)\noof_top1 = oof_order[:, 0]\noof_top3 = oof_order[:, :3]\n\nwrong_top1 = np.where(oof_top1 != ytr_full)[0]\nmiss_top3 = np.array([i for i in range(len(ytr_full)) if ytr_full[i] not in oof_top3[i]])\n\nprint(f\"Top-1 errors: {len(wrong_top1)} / {len(ytr_full)} ({len(wrong_top1)/len(ytr_full):.1%})\")\nprint(f\"MAP@3 total misses: {len(miss_top3)} / {len(ytr_full)} ({len(miss_top3)/len(ytr_full):.1%})\")\n\nerror_examples = train.iloc[miss_top3[:10]].copy()\nerror_examples['true_answer'] = [OPTS[ytr_full[i]] for i in miss_top3[:10]]\nerror_examples['ensemble_top3'] = [' '.join(OPTS[j] for j in oof_top3[i]) for i in miss_top3[:10]]\nerror_examples[['prompt', 'true_answer', 'ensemble_top3']]\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"bbebb5b1","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 10. Final Kaggle Submission","metadata":{}},{"id":"05b6aef2","cell_type":"code","source":"\ntest_probs_ens = ensemble_probs(w, test_probs_m1, test_probs_m2, test_probs_m3)\npreds = top3_labels(test_probs_ens)\nsubmission = pd.DataFrame({\"ID\": test['id'], \"Prediction\": preds})\nsubmission.to_csv(\"submission.csv\", index=False)\nsubmission.head()\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"5911bf89","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 11. Notes / Honesty Check\n\n- OOF MAP@3 from Section 8 is your best honest estimate of the leaderboard score —\n  it's computed the same way as the actual metric, on data the models never trained on.\n- If OOF MAP@3 doesn't reach ~0.78, the retrieval corpus quality and Model 3's context length\n  are the first things to check — a weak or off-domain corpus can *hurt* MAP@3 by diluting\n  the input with irrelevant passages. Try `top_k=1` or a domain-matched corpus if so.\n- 5-fold CV means Model 3 now trains **5x** — budget GPU time/quota accordingly (this is the\n  main tradeoff of this approach: better, more honest numbers, but slower to run).\n- Keep the v1 notebook's leakage-free submission logic as the baseline in your report so you\n  can show the score progression (v1 → v2) as evidence of genuine iteration, not a lucky guess.\n","metadata":{}}]}